WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<b>Calpis theater</b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Subs: English

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
S

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.350
The Burnt Letter

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.640
<i>Recently, Peter is in a bad mood.</i>

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.740
<i>Heidi is only thinking
about taking care of Pichi,</i>

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.170
<i>and she no longer goes with him
up to the mountain pastures.</i>

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.230
<i>Peter feels very bored.</i>

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.800
Hey, Peter!

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.450
Wait for me!

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.210
Listen, can you deliver this letter to Alm-Uncle?

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:24.710
To Alm-Uncle?

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.320
All right? Don't forget.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.780
I am grateful for your help.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.550
This way I do not need to
climb the mountain to the cabin.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.580
And I don't need to see the face of
Alm-Uncle, isn't that true?

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.280
Then I'm counting on you.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.420
Are you all right?
Pichi, hang in there!

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.650
Come on, one more time.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:15.510
See?

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:19.940
Yes, like that!
Flap your wings!

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.440
Joseph, he's falling!

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.140
Thank goodness.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.810
Come on, let's try again.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.940
Heidi, you shouldn't force
him to fly so much.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.810
He'll soon learn to fly by himself.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.840
Whoa! That was dangerous.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.300
He flew so far.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.400
He flew from over there.
Amazing!

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.960
Grandfather,
he's almost there, isn't he?

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.570
Just a little more and
he will be able to fly.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.810
Yes, it seems he will
be able to fly soon.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.270
But let him rest for now.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.000
Pichi, just one more time.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.680
Snowflake, be quiet.
Heidi prefers to be with Pichi.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.950
Snowflake!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.140
Peter.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:32.380
Pichi flew!
He can fly!

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.600
See?

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.340
See, Snowflake?

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.820
You're not coming with us
to the mountains?

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:45.880
What?

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.340
Pichi!

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:52.350
Darn!

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:56.510
Let's go.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.560
Peter.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.830
Curses, curses, curses!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.950
Pichi, Pichi!
That's all she cares about!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:13.860
Curses!

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.500
The letter to Alm-Uncle.
I forgot to give it to him!

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.350
Wait!

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.460
Hey, wait for me!

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:37.600
It's all Heidi's fault!
Heidi! Heidi's the one to blame!

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:45.380
Grandfather, I'm going today.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.280
I'm going!
Give me my lunch.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.720
Will Pichi be all right?

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.780
He's coming with me.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.160
He can fly now.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.500
Hurry up!

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.360
Peter!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.940
Pichi, one day you will be
able to fly as well as those birds.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.340
Well? You will. Won't you?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:45.880
Pichi!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.170
You are getting better.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.170
Come on, we're almost there.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:56.900
Let's go.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.810
Peter!

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.070
Peter!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.730
Heidi.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.400
Peter!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.540
Peter, look!
Pichi came, too!

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:20.680
Catch him.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.420
All right!

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.140
He flies very well, doesn't he?

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.300
Doesn't he look so
pretty when he flies?

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.820
Why didn't you tell
me you would come?

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.150
If you had, I would have waited.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.990
Why are you angry?

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:43.570
Peter!

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.770
Here.
I forgot to give it to Alm-Uncle.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.930
What's that?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.240
It's a letter.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.860
And it's all your fault, Heidi.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:04.530
Forget it.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.990
I'm afraid, but I'll give
him when we get back.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.160
There's nothing I can do.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:13.820
I forgot.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.080
Here!
It's your lunch.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:19.830
A big slice of cheese and bread.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.130
Can I eat it?

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.160
I can't eat everything alone.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:28.400
I see!

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.390
He is cute.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.890
All right, Pichi. Let's go!

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.170
Come on, fly!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.080
Pichi, hang in there!

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:57.540
The Goat General Peter

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:57.540
Yagi no taishou peetaa

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.460
All right, now even higher!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:06.520
He can get angry, but is truly kind-hearted.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:06.520
Okottemo honto ha yasashii peetaa

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:07.300
<i>Peter is very happy that Heidi has
come back to the mountain again.</i>

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:13.080
The two of us shared and ate

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:13.080
Futari de chiizu to pan wo

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:11.770
<i>It's not only because he gets his lunch.</i>

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:16.650
<i>The days when Heidi hadn't come,
he couldn't help feeling bored.</i>

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.640
cheese and bread together,

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.640
Wakete tabeta no ne

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:30.260
on the day the bellflowers swayed.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:30.260
Tsuri ga nesou ga yureteita hi

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.300
Go!

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.850
Fly, fly.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:38.600
- Pichi!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.680
Higher, higher!

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:52.850
Higher, fly higher!

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.710
Pichi, fly even higher!

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.070
Pichi, enough!

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:28.650
Come back here!

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:30.620
Rest a little, Pichi!

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.120
Pichi!

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.110
The hawk!

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.180
Heidi, the hawk!
Hurry and catch Pichi!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.640
Don't, Pichi!

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.190
Hurry!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.770
Hurry and catch him!

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.330
<i>Ouch, that hurt.</i>

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.370
Peter, are you all right?

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.480
It's only a scratch.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.860
Look! I'm a hawk.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.300
Peter!

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.730
Thank you, Peter.
You are so strong.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:02.330
What was that?

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:07.740
It was my belly.
It seems like it's empty.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:09.590
Mine, too!

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.330
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat!

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.480
He wants to eat, too.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:25.970
Now you're very quiet, but
you were scared of the hawk.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:29.390
How friendly.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.500
Come on!

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:36.770
Let's go!

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.260
Snowflake is missing.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:05.940
What?

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.540
Little Swan and Little Bear are also missing.
Don't you see them anywhere?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.250
Snowflake!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.970
Little Bear!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.780
Little Swan!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.100
I don't see them.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.840
Heidi, stay here.
I'm going to search for them.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:35.340
I'm going, too!

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:39.110
Little Swan!

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.900
Snowflake!

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.220
Little Bear!

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.620
Little Bear!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.320
Snowflake!

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.650
<i>Something terrible has happened.</i>

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:49.150
Snowflake!

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.160
Little Swan!

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:51.300
<i>While they were playing with Pichi,</i>

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:55.520
<i>the goats Little Swan, Little Bear and Snowflake disappeared.</i>

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.180
Little Swan!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.930
Snowflake!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:58.080
Snowflake!

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.810
Little Bear!

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.420
Little Bear!

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.180
Little Swan!

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.180
Little Swan!

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.350
Snowflake!

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.770
They disappeared.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.560
Over there, there are some
rocks that taste like salt.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.130
So, they are over there?

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:26.220
Maybe.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:26.920
Let's go.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:39.720
Fog. Hurry.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.340
The fog is getting thicker.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.290
Little Bear!

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:07.300
Snowflake!

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.400
Are we still far from the
rocks that taste like salt?

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:12.840
We must be close to them.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.680
But I can't see them.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.910
Little Swan!

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:30.860
In this fog, we'll never find
Snowflake and the others!

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.130
What are we going to do?

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:46.870
I'm scared.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.790
That's why I told you to stay with the herd.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:51.830
Peter...

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:01.310
Peter!

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:02.460
Where are you?

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:05.220
Peter!

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.100
- I'm right here!

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:11.900
This only happened because you
were always playing with Pichi!

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.290
You're blaming me, too, Peter?

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.290
Shh!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.360
Snowflake!

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.770
It seems that they
really came here.

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:23.970
Come on, give me your hand.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:24.640
All right.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.100
Snowflake!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.460
Snowflake!

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.280
Little Swan!

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.280
Little Swan!

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:30.330
Little Bear!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:31.440
Little Bear!

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:37.140
Snowflake!

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:40.240
Snowflake!

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.200
Snowflake!

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.170
Heidi, don't drift away.

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:58.010
Yes.

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:00.680
Everything's all right now.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:04.490
We just have to follow Peter
until we find the others.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:08.450
Huh?

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:15.240
What's wrong?

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.700
I thought that the tree we
crossed before was over here.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:21.380
Then where could it be?
That way?

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.370
No. I think we are lost.

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:31.280
What should we do?
Should we turn back?

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:35.090
It's dangerous.
For now we should stay here.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:36.420
Let's rest.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.560
In a place like this?

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.350
We don't have a choice.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.990
I wonder if the other goats are all right.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:01.190
What do you think, Peter?

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:05.000
I'm worried too,
but there's nothing I can do.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:19.370
Pichi, what's wrong?

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.130
It's Joseph! Joseph!

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:33.540
Joseph!
Joseph, we are here!

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:39.310
Joseph!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.110
Joseph!

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:21.580
We're back.

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:28.880
Alm-Uncle!

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.130
Grandfather!

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:33.720
You're finally back.

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:35.390
Grandfather!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.730
Grandfather.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:49.730
The fog got thicker,
so I came to get you.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:51.750
What happened here, General?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:57.980
Well... Little Swan, Little Bear and
Snowflake got lost...

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:04.750
It's not Peter's fault.
Pichi got scared of the hawk...

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:07.690
And then you lost them.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:09.180
Yes.

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:15.130
Peter saved him!
Pichi almost got eaten.

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:17.460
I see.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:21.110
Anyway, you two
must be hungry.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:21.570
Here.

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:28.770
Now that I think about it,
we haven't had lunch yet.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:34.120
Again!

00:20:56.560 --> 00:21:01.230
Hey, hey, General!
You'll choke if you eat that fast!

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:08.190
I told you so.

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:17.530
Oh, Peter!
You always eat too fast.

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:21.800
Oh, that's right, I'm sorry for forgetting.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:24.930
I was asked to deliver a letter to you.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:26.000
To me?

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:28.250
Yes, here it is.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.390
Dete!

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.060
All right, go on, eat.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.970
Joseph. Goodnight.

00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:04.250
Goodnight, Grandfather.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:08.360
Yes, you are very tired today,
you'll sleep well tonight.

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:09.110
Yes.

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:10.560
Good night.

00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:29.000
"I am now working and am in good health."<i></i>

00:22:29.590 --> 00:22:31.690
<i>"Frankfurt is a very nice place."</i>

00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:36.270
<i>"I would like for Heidi to go
to school in such a city."</i>

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:45.910
Grandfather.

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:49.020
W-what is it?

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:53.080
What's wrong?

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:58.640
You know, today when I saw
you in the mountains, I was very happy.

00:22:58.640 --> 00:22:59.440
Good night.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:02.480
Heidi...

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:19.420
<i>The letter is from Aunt Dete
who brought Heidi to the mountain.</i>

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.300
<i>It says she wants to come for her some time.</i>

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:27.210
<i>But for the old man,
the letter is of no concern.</i>

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:29.650
<i>Little by little,</i>

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:35.460
<i>Heidi has become important to him,
and he won't let anyone take her.</i>

00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:59.370
<i>Summer is almost over, and Heidi has
adjusted to life on the mountain.</i>

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:03.230
<i>She wants to become a goatherd
like Peter, and she won't give up.</i>

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:08.150
<i>She tries to milk the goats,
just like Grandfather, but it doesn't go well.</i>

00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:12.880
<i>She wants to learn to whistle just
like Peter, so she can call the goats,</i>

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:15.170
<i>but only a strange sound comes out.</i>

00:24:15.380 --> 00:24:19.460
<i>One day, when Heidi goes
to the mountain as usual,</i>

00:24:19.460 --> 00:24:22.290
<i>Peter suddenly gets a stomach ache,</i>

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:24.890
<i>and she gets really scared.</i>

00:24:25.220 --> 00:24:27.810
<i>Next episode:
Whistle Louder</i>

